# Signal — Always-On Core Guardrails

You are collaborating in parallel on **Signal** (by **Signal Design, Inc.**): Pure Rust EDA engine in K8s + Node.js 22 BFF + Angular 19/20+ Zoneless Web IDE.

## 1. Sources of Truth & Phase Gate
- **Canonical Rulebook:** [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) | **Specs:** `architecture/01..18-*.md` | **Guides:** `docs/engineering/*.md` | **Skills:** `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md`.
- **Phase Gate:** Check `AGENTS.md` Section 1 and `coordination/TASK_BOARD.md`. Never write production code (`engine/`, `services/`, `web/`, `ai/`, `contracts/`, `infra/`) before explicit Phase 0 user approval.
- **Session Start:** Run `git fetch origin --prune`, read `coordination/TASK_BOARD.md`, peer journal (`coordination/agents/antigravity.md` read-only for Cursor), and `coordination/handoffs/`. Branch `cursor/<task-id>-<slug>` or `contract/<task-id>-<slug>` with zero `touched_paths` overlap.
- **Single-Writer Journals:** Cursor edits ONLY `coordination/agents/cursor.md`; Antigravity edits ONLY `coordination/agents/antigravity.md`.

## 2. Hard Red-Line Invariants (PR Rejection If Violated)
1. **1 Project = 1 Security Cell:** PostgreSQL RLS (`NOBYPASSRLS`), 3-Tier `pgvector` HNSW, per-project Hybrid PQC (`ML-KEM-768` + 2-level `HKDF`) DEK & SPIFFE SVID, `< 8 MB` `signal-cell-wasm` (`EXPLORER`) or Kata/`CONFIDENTIAL_SILICON` + Exclusive `H100 CC` / Blackwell `B200 TEE-I/O` MIG, Cilium eBPF 100% lateral drop, uniform `404` anti-enumeration, and socket-pinned + epoch-fencing `signal-egress-proxy`.
2. **Rust Owns All Physics & Manufacturing:** Zero SPICE, magnetics, creepage, EMC/FMEDA, DRC/LVS, routing, ECO, or Gerber/GDSII/IPC-2581 logic in Node.js or Angular.
3. **Zero Local Design Files & No Browser Export/Print:** Never persist design IP in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`/`IndexedDB`/SW caches or expose `/export`, `/download`, or `/print` routes. All physical manufacturing/MCAD/regulatory/nailboard bundles egress ONLY via Step-Up 2FA write-only `russh` SFTP.
4. **BYO-Git, Padmé-Blinded Vault & Universal Parts (`18-*`):** Customer owns design repos (`GitHub`/`GitLab`/`Bitbucket`: `<project>-meta` + lazy `<project>-<type>` bound by `provider_repo_id`) + Org-private `<org>/signal-org-parts` AVL overlays under Padmé-blinded RFC 8452 `AES-256-GCM-SIV` + Dual-Fenced 2PC `Super-Commit`; never hardcode pad polygons outside `PadstackDef` or leak NDA parts into Global CAS.
5. **Contract-First `bigint` Safety:** All 64-bit integer contract fields (`_nm`, `_ps`, `fencing_epoch`) use `[jstype = JS_STRING]` / ES2020 `bigint` (`longAsBigint: true`). Generate stubs at build time ONLY (never commit generated stubs).
6. **Zero-Bypass Local Dev:** `dev-guest-auth` (`local-guest-0001`) executes full RBAC + encryption and MUST fail compilation in release/staging builds.

## 3. Token Efficiency, 2–3 Sentence Dev Replies & Anti-Hallucination
- **2–3 Sentence Coding Replies:** During code development/bug-fixing, reply in **2–3 sentences max** stating ONLY the issue, exact fix applied, and verification result—no verbose recaps or repeated diffs unless explicitly asked.
- **Zero-Hallucination Discipline:** Always verify paths, symbols, versions (`Cargo.toml`/`package.json`), and contracts via `rg`/`view_file` before editing; NEVER claim tests/builds pass without observing exit code `0`; NEVER invent pinouts/SI constants; stop and ask (or log `BLOCKED_ON_CONTRACT`) when ambiguous.
- **Clean Modularity:** Files `<= 300 LOC` (split `> 350 LOC`), functions `<= 40 LOC`, nesting `<= 3`, 3-line module header; load scoped `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` and `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md` on demand.
